---
import FlowDetail from '../FlowDetail.astro';
import { FLOW_V16_SHOTS as shots } from '../../../data/flow-v16';
---
<section class="border-t border-border/60 px-6 py-14 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="tour-routing"><div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
  <div><p class="of-eyebrow">Smart Routing</p><h3 id="tour-routing" class="of-display scroll-mt-28 mt-4 text-[clamp(1.85rem,3.4vw,2.75rem)]">Your rules choose. Flow shows why.</h3><p class="of-lede mt-5">Rules decide in order; the first one that fits the request applies. Six built-in rules cover local speed, exact chart and table output, locality, document fit and cost. Duplicate a rule to edit it.</p><p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-text-muted">One sentence names the model, followed by “Decided by the rule.” Choose a model yourself and no rule takes credit. Flow Runtime comes first in the default provider order.</p><p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-text-muted">A rule with no qualifying model says so. Unmeasured models are not speed-ranked, missing prices are never guessed, and rules never judge answer quality.</p><a href="/flow/settings/#smart-routing" class="of-text-action mt-6 inline-flex">Explore Smart Routing <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
  <FlowDetail src={shots.settingsRouting} alt="Six Smart Routing rules with the deciding rule marked and the chosen model named." caption="Captured September 6, 2026 · Installed Flow 1.6 (1899) · The model and deciding rule stay together" />
</div></section>
